# Shattered Forge — Main Menu Contract Rule

## Source of truth
- Treat `Docs/ShatteredForge/Menu_logic_contract.md` as the **canonical behavioral contract** for the start menu, profiles, and expedition resume rules.
- Treat `Docs/ShatteredForge/Menu_logic_contract.md` “Glossary (RU UI ↔ EN canonical)” as the **canonical naming map** between Russian UI strings and English identifiers used in docs/code comments.

## Required workflow (menu/profile changes)
- Before changing behavior: read/reconcile with `Menu_logic_contract.md` (especially invariants + scenario IDs).
- After changing behavior: update `Menu_logic_contract.md` in the same PR/session (scenarios/decision table/status labels) so docs never lag code.
- If UX copy is Russian but identifiers are English: keep English identifiers stable; update RU labels in UI and mirror mapping in the glossary table if needed.

## Non-negotiables (do not regress)
- First launch with no profiles: only `New Game`, `Settings`, `Quit Game` (no `Continue`).
- Active profile must be shown as a corner entry/button and open profile actions (switch/create).
- `Continue` should eventually map to real expedition resume semantics; prototype fallback to scene reload/start is acceptable only if documented in `Menu_logic_contract.md`.
- Never write stale `PlayerPrefs["sf.active_profile_id"]` after profile deletion; keep profile index + prefs consistent.

## QA hook
- When validating menu wiring, prefer running `MenuContractSmokeTestRunner` / editor smoke menu item described in `Docs/ShatteredForge/Main_menu_setup.md` (if present in the repo).
